# Luna Agents - environment variables.
#
# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in. Server-side only. Per
# travelgenix-security: no secret here is ever exposed to the browser, and the
# service-role key bypasses RLS so it must never ship client-side. Only values
# prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ reach the browser, and none of those are secrets.

# --- Supabase (Stage 2 persistence) ---
# The opportunity table lives here. Service-role key is server-only.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Review digest links (Stage 2) ---
# Base URL the approve / edit / reject links point at. Defaults to localhost in dev.
REVIEW_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Luna email composer (Stage 2 drafting, not wired yet) ---
# The composer runs in the Luna Marketing app. Add the re-engagement archetype there,
# then call it from here. Auth model is still being decided (cookie session today;
# a service-to-service path is needed for the unattended weekly run).
# COMPOSER_BASE_URL=
# COMPOSER_SERVICE_TOKEN=

# --- Sending (Stage 3, post-approval only) ---
# The client's own sender identity (Brevo or their mail). No autonomous send.
# BREVO_API_KEY=
